From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] server: log PS4 server-directory identity mismatch

On PS4, create_server_dir reaches the requested prefix and successfully
changes into the new server directory, but Wine's path stat and cwd fstat
identity check fails. Log both dev/inode pairs and continue on Prospero so the
next startup stage can be observed. Keep Wine's strict check on other
platforms; the reason for the PS4 metadata mismatch remains to be determined.
---
diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -1183,7 +1183,20 @@
     if (fstat( server_dir_fd, &st2 ) == -1)
         fatal_error( "stat %s: %s\n", server_dir, strerror( errno ));
     if (st.st_dev != st2.st_dev || st.st_ino != st2.st_ino)
+    {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        extern int sceKernelDebugOutText( int channel, const char *text );
+        char line[192];
+
+        snprintf( line, sizeof(line),
+                  "wineserver: server-dir identity differs dev=%llx/%llx ino=%llx/%llx\n",
+                  (unsigned long long)st.st_dev, (unsigned long long)st2.st_dev,
+                  (unsigned long long)st.st_ino, (unsigned long long)st2.st_ino );
+        sceKernelDebugOutText( 0, line );
+#else
         fatal_error( "chdir did not end up in %s\n", server_dir );
+#endif
+    }
 
     free( base_dir );
     free( config_dir );
-- 
